# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage
.playwright-cli/
output/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# generated résumé PDFs
# These are build outputs — `npm run build` renders /resume in headless Chrome and
# writes them before next build collects public/. Tracking them made a silent
# failure available: the committed blob went stale whenever the résumé changed, and
# once shipped carrying a test probe string that only existed in a working tree.
# The build is the only thing that should produce them.
/public/resume.pdf
/public/resume-a4.pdf
/public/resume.meta.json

# agent instruction files — local only
# This repo is linked from /projects as a public work sample, so the tooling that
# helps build it does not belong in it. AGENTS.md is regenerated by `next dev`
# (see node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js), which is why it
# needs ignoring rather than just deleting — otherwise it returns on every dev run.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
